#: ../../source/start-here.rst-1
msgid ""
"The best way to get started with Diátaxis is by applying it to documentation"
" problems."
msgstr "入门 Diátaxis 的最好办法，就是把它用到文档问题上。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:7
msgid "Start here - Diátaxis in five minutes"
msgstr "从这里开始——五分钟了解 Diátaxis"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:11
msgid ""
"Treat this website as a handbook or a toolbox that you make use of when you "
"need it."
msgstr "把本网站当作一本手册、一只工具箱，需要时取用。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:13
msgid ""
"You don't need to read everything on this website to make sense of Diátaxis,"
" or to start using it in practice. In fact I recommend that you don't. **The"
" best way to get started with Diátaxis is by applying it** - to something, "
"however small."
msgstr "要理解 Diátaxis、要在实践中用上它，你都不必读遍本网站的所有内容。其实我建议"
"你别读。**入门 Diátaxis 的最好办法，就是把它用起来**——用在什么东西上都行，多"
"小都行。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:15
msgid ""
"Read this page for a brief primer. Each section contains links to more in-"
"depth material; refer to that when you need it - when you're actually at "
"work, or reflecting on the documentation problems you have encountered."
msgstr "读读本页，当作一份简明入门。每一节都链接了更深入的材料；需要时再去查阅——在你"
"真正工作的时候，或是在反思自己遇到的文档问题时。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:20
msgid "The four kinds of documentation"
msgstr "四类文档"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:22
msgid ""
"The core idea of Diátaxis is that there are fundamentally four identifiable "
"kinds of documentation, that respond to four different needs. The four kinds"
" are: *tutorials*, *how-to guides*, *reference* and *explanation*. Each has "
"a different purpose, and needs to be written in a different way."
msgstr "Diátaxis 的核心思想是：文档从根本上说有四种可辨识的类型，回应四种不同的需求"
"。这四种类型是：*教程*、*实践指南*、*参考资料*和*解释说明*。每一种都有不同的"
"目的，也要用不同的方式去写。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:26
msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr "教程"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:30
msgid ":ref:`Tutorials in more detail <tutorials>`"
msgstr ":ref:`教程详解 <tutorials>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:31
msgid ""
":ref:`Why tutorials are completely different from how-to guides <tutorials-"
"how-to>`"
msgstr ":ref:`教程为何与实践指南截然不同 <tutorials-how-to>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:33
msgid ""
"**A tutorial is a lesson**, that takes a student by the hand through a "
"learning experience. A tutorial is always *practical*: the user *does* "
"something, under the guidance of an instructor. A tutorial is designed "
"around an encounter that the learner can make sense of, in which the "
"instructor is responsible for the learner's safety and success."
msgstr "**教程是一堂课**，牵着学生的手，带他走完一段学习经历。教程始终是*实践性*的："
"用户在讲师的指引下*亲自动手*。教程围绕一次学习者能够理解的相遇来设计，在这次"
"相遇中，讲师要为学习者的安全与成功负责。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:35
msgid ""
"A driving lesson is a good example of a tutorial. The purpose of the lesson "
"is to develop skills and confidence in the student, not to get from A to B. "
"A software example could be: *Let's create a simple game in Python*."
msgstr "驾驶课就是教程的好例子。这堂课的目的，是培养学生的技能与信心，而不是从 A 开"
"到 B。软件领域的例子可以是：*我们用 Python 做一个小游戏*。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:37
msgid ""
"*The user will learn through what they do* - not because someone has tried "
"to teach them."
msgstr "*用户会在自己动手做的过程中学习*——而不是因为有人试图教他们。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:39
msgid ""
"In documentation, the special difficulty is that the instructor is condemned"
" to be absent, and is not there to monitor the learner and correct their "
"mistakes. The instructor must somehow find a way to be present through "
"written instruction alone."
msgstr "在文档中，特殊的困难在于：讲师注定缺席，无法在场观察学习者、纠正他们的错误。"
"讲师必须设法仅凭书面讲解，让自己仍然在场。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:43
msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr "实践指南"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:47
msgid ":ref:`How-to guides in more detail <how-to>`"
msgstr ":ref:`实践指南详解 <how-to>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:49
msgid ""
"**A how-to guide addresses a real-world goal or problem**, by providing "
"practical directions to help the user who is in that situation."
msgstr "**实践指南面向现实世界中的目标或问题**，给出切实可行的指引，帮助身处那种情境"
"的用户。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:51
msgid ""
"A how-to guide always addresses an already-competent user, who is expected "
"to be able to use the guide to help them get their work done. In contrast to"
" a tutorial, a how-to guide is concerned with *work* rather than *study*."
msgstr "实践指南总是面向已经具备相应能力的用户，他们理应能借助这份指南完成自己的工作"
"。与教程不同，实践指南关心的是*工作*，而不是*学习*。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:53
msgid ""
"A how-to guide might be: *How to store cellulose nitrate film* (in motion "
"picture photography) or *How to configure frame profiling* (in software). Or"
" even: *Troubleshooting deployment problems*."
msgstr "实践指南可能是：*如何保存硝酸纤维素胶片*（电影摄影），或者*如何配置帧性能分"
"析*（软件）。甚至可能是：*排查部署问题*。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:57
msgid "Reference"
msgstr "参考资料"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:61
msgid ":ref:`Reference in more detail <reference>`"
msgstr ":ref:`参考资料详解 <reference>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:63
msgid ""
"**Reference guides contain the technical description** - facts - that a user"
" needs in order to do things correctly: accurate, complete, reliable "
"information, free of distraction and interpretation. They contain "
"*propositional or theoretical knowledge*, not guides to action."
msgstr "**参考资料包含技术描述**——即事实——也就是用户要把事情做对所需要的东西：准确、"
"完整、可靠的信息，不夹带干扰，也不夹带阐释。它承载的是*命题性或理论性知识*，"
"而不是行动指南。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:65
msgid ""
"Like a how-to guide, reference documentation serves the user who is at "
"*work*, and it's up to the user to be sufficiently competent to interpret "
"and use it correctly."
msgstr "和实践指南一样，参考资料服务于处于*工作*状态的用户；能否正确解读并使用它，全"
"看用户自己是否足够胜任。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:67
msgid ""
"*Reference material is neutral.* It is not concerned with what the user is "
"doing. A marine chart could be used by a ship's navigator to plot a course, "
"but equally well by an investigating judge."
msgstr "*参考资料是中立的。*它不关心用户正在做什么。航海图可以供船上的领航员规划航线"
"，也同样可以供调查法官使用。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:69
msgid ""
"Where possible, the architecture of reference documentation should reflect "
"the structure or architecture of the thing it's describing - just like a map"
" does. If a method is part of a class that belongs to a certain module, then"
" we should expect to see the same relationship in the documentation too."
msgstr "只要可能，参考资料的架构就应当反映它所描述之物的结构或架构——就像地图那样。如"
"果一个方法属于某个类，而这个类又属于某个模块，那么在文档中，我们也应当看到同"
"样的关系。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:73
msgid "Explanation"
msgstr "解释说明"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:77
msgid ":ref:`Explanation in more detail <explanation>`"
msgstr ":ref:`解释说明详解 <explanation>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:78
msgid ""
":ref:`Understanding the difference between reference and explanation "
"<reference-explanation>`"
msgstr ":ref:`理解参考资料与解释说明的区别 <reference-explanation>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:81
msgid ""
"**Explanatory guides provide context and background.** They serve the need "
"to understand and put things in a bigger picture. Explanation joins things "
"together, and helps answer the question *why?*"
msgstr "**解释说明提供语境与背景。**它的用处，是帮人理解事物，把事物放进更大的图景里"
"。解释说明把事物联结起来，帮助回答*为什么？*这个问题。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:83
msgid ""
"Explanation often needs to circle around its subject, and approach it from "
"different directions. It can contain opinions and take perspectives."
msgstr "解释说明往往需要围绕主题盘旋，从不同方向切入。它可以包含观点，也可以采取不同"
"的视角。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:85
msgid ""
"Like reference, explanation belongs to the realm of propositional knowledge "
"rather than action. However its purpose is to serve the user's study - as "
"tutorials do - and not their work."
msgstr "与参考资料一样，解释说明属于命题性知识的领域，而非行动。但它的目的在于服务用"
"户的学习——如同教程那样——而不是用户的工作。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:87
msgid ""
"Often, writers of tutorials who are anxious that their students should "
"*know* things overload their tutorials with distracting and unhelpful "
"explanation. It would be much more useful to give the learner the most "
"minimal explanation (\"Here, we use HTTPS because it's safer\") and then "
"link to an in-depth article (*Secure communication using HTTPS encryption*) "
"for when the user is ready for it."
msgstr "教程作者常担心学生不*知道*某些东西，于是往教程里塞满分散注意力、毫无助益的解"
"释。远为有用的做法，是先给学习者最精简的解释（“这里用 HTTPS，因为它更安全”）"
"，再链接一篇深入的文章（*使用 HTTPS 加密的安全通信*），等用户准备好时再去读"
"。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:93
msgid "The Diátaxis map"
msgstr "Diátaxis 地图"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:95
msgid ""
"The four kinds of documentation and the relationships between them can be "
"summarised in the Diátaxis map."
msgstr "四类文档及其相互关系，可以用 Diátaxis 地图来概括。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:99
msgid ":ref:`The map in more detail <map>`"
msgstr ":ref:`地图详解 <map>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:101
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is not just a list of four different things, but a conceptual "
"arrangement of them. It shows how the four kinds of documentation are "
"related to each other, and distinct from each other."
msgstr "Diátaxis 不只是四种不同东西的清单，更是对它们的概念性排布。它展示了四类文档"
"彼此之间如何关联、又如何区分。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:103
msgid ""
"Crossing or blurring the boundaries described in the map is at the heart of "
"a vast number of problems in documentation."
msgstr "跨越或模糊地图所描绘的边界，正是大量文档问题的核心症结。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:105
msgid "Diátaxis"
msgstr "Diátaxis"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:112
msgid "The Diátaxis compass"
msgstr "Diátaxis 指南针"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:114
msgid "As you can see from the map:"
msgstr "从地图中可以看出："

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:116
msgid ""
"tutorials and how-to guides are concerned with what the user *does* "
"(**action**)"
msgstr "教程和实践指南，关注的是用户*做什么*（**行（行动）**）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:117
msgid ""
"reference and explanation are about what the user *knows* (**cognition**)"
msgstr "参考资料和解释说明，关注的是用户*知道什么*（**知（认知）**）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:119
msgid "On the other hand:"
msgstr "另一方面："

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:121
msgid ""
"tutorials and explanation serve the *acquisition* of skill (the user's "
"**study**)"
msgstr "教程和解释说明，服务于技能的*习得*（用户的**学**）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:122
msgid ""
"how-to guides and reference serve the *application* of skill (the user's "
"**work**)"
msgstr "实践指南和参考资料，服务于技能的*应用*（用户的**用**）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:124
msgid ""
"But a map doesn't tell you what to *do* - it's reference. To guide your "
"action you need a different sort of tool, in this case, a kind of Diátaxis "
"compass."
msgstr "但地图不会告诉你该*怎么做*——它本身就是参考资料。要引导行动，你需要另一种工具"
"；在这里，也就是一种 Diátaxis 指南针。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:128
msgid ":ref:`The compass in more detail <compass>`"
msgstr ":ref:`指南针详解 <compass>`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:130
msgid "The compass is useful in two different ways."
msgstr "指南针有两种不同的用途。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:132
msgid ""
"When creating documentation, it helps clarify your own intentions, and helps"
" make sure you're actually doing what you think you're doing."
msgstr "创建文档时，它能帮你厘清自己的意图，也能帮你确认：你做的，确实就是你以为自己"
"在做的事。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:134
msgid ""
"When looking at documentation, it helps understand what's going on in it, "
"and makes problems stand out."
msgstr "审视文档时，它能帮你理解其中的状况，并让问题凸显出来。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:136
msgid ""
"The compass is not nearly as eye-catching as the map, but when you're at "
"work puzzling over a documentation problem it's what will help you move "
"forward."
msgstr "指南针远不如地图醒目，但当你在工作中为一个文档问题苦苦琢磨时，能让你往前走的"
"，正是它。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:144
msgid "If the content..."
msgstr "如果内容……"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:145
msgid "...and serves the user's..."
msgstr "……服务于用户的……"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:146
msgid "...then it must belong to..."
msgstr "……那么它必然属于……"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:147 ../../source/start-here.rst:150
msgid "informs action"
msgstr "指导行动（行）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:148 ../../source/start-here.rst:157
msgid "acquisition of skill"
msgstr "技能的习得（学）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:149
msgid "a tutorial"
msgstr "教程"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:151 ../../source/start-here.rst:154
msgid "application of skill"
msgstr "技能的应用（用）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:152
msgid "a how-to guide"
msgstr "实践指南"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:153 ../../source/start-here.rst:156
msgid "informs cognition"
msgstr "帮助认知（知）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:155
msgid "reference"
msgstr "参考资料"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:158
msgid "explanation"
msgstr "解释说明"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:165
msgid "Working"
msgstr "动手做"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:167
msgid "There is a very simple workflow for Diátaxis."
msgstr "Diátaxis 有一套十分简单的工作流程。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:171
msgid ":ref:`how-to-use-diataxis`"
msgstr ":ref:`how-to-use-diataxis`"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:173
msgid ""
"Consider what you see in the documentation, in front of you right now (which"
" might be literally nothing, if you haven't started yet)."
msgstr "想一想你此刻在眼前的文档中看到了什么（如果你还没开始，那可能真的什么也没有）"
"。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:175
msgid "Ask: *is there any way in which it could be improved?*"
msgstr "问一问：*有没有什么办法能让它变得更好？*"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:177
msgid ""
"Decide on *one* thing you could do to it right now, however small, that "
"would improve it."
msgstr "定下此刻就能对它做的*一件*事，无论多小，只要能改进它就好。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:179
msgid "Do that thing."
msgstr "去做那件事。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:181
msgid "And then repeat."
msgstr "然后再重复。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:183
msgid "That's it."
msgstr "就是这样。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:189
msgid "Do what you like"
msgstr "随你所用"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:191
msgid ""
"You can do what you like with Diátaxis. You don't have to believe in it and "
"there is no exam. It is a wholly pragmatic approach. I think it's *true*, "
"but what matters is that it actually helps people create better "
"documentation. If you find one idea or insight in it that seems to be "
"worthwhile, help yourself to that."
msgstr "Diátaxis，你想怎么用就怎么用。你不必相信它，也没有考试。它完全是一种务实的方"
"法。我认为它是*对的*，但真正要紧的是，它确实能帮人写出更好的文档。如果你在其"
"中发现一个看起来有价值的想法或洞见，尽管拿去用。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:193
msgid ""
"There is an extensively elaborated theory around Diátaxis, but you don't "
"need to subscribe to it, or even read about it. Diátaxis doesn't require a "
"commitment to pursue it to a final end."
msgstr "Diátaxis 背后有一套阐发详尽的理论，但你无须认同它，甚至无须去读。Diátaxis 不"
"要求你承诺把它贯彻到底。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:195
msgid ""
"You can do just one thing, right now, and even if you do nothing else ever "
"after, you will at least have made that one improvement. (In practice what "
"you will find is that each thing you do will give you a clue as to the next "
"thing to do - you only need to keep doing them.)"
msgstr "此刻，你只做一件事就行；哪怕此后再也不做别的，至少也已经做成了这一项改进。（"
"实践中你会发现：每做一件事，都会带来下一件事的线索——你只需要一直做下去。）"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:199
msgid "Get started"
msgstr "开始吧"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:201
msgid ""
"At this point, you have read everything you need to get started with "
"Diátaxis."
msgstr "到这里，你已经读完了入门 Diátaxis 所需的全部内容。"

#: ../../source/start-here.rst:203
msgid ""
"You can read more if you want, and eventually you probably should, but *you "
"will get the most value from the guidance in this website when you turn to "
"it with a problem or a question*. That's when it comes alive."
msgstr "你愿意的话，可以接着往下读——早晚你大概也该读。不过，*当你带着一个问题或疑问"
"来查阅本网站的指引时，你会从中获得最大的价值*。也就是在那一刻，它才真正活了"
"过来。"
